    "abstract": "RetNet is a foundation architecture for large language models that achieves training parallelism, low-cost inference, and good performance. The retention mechanism supports three computation paradigms: parallel (for training), recurrent (O(1) inference), and chunkwise recurrent (linear-complexity long-sequence modelling). RetNet achieves favourable scaling results, parallel training, low-cost deployment, and efficient inference compared with Transformers.",
    "domain": "NLP",
    "key_claims": [
      "Retention can be computed in parallel, recurrent, and chunkwise-recurrent forms that are mathematically equivalent.",
      "Multi-scale decay rates gamma = 1 - 2^(-5-i) per head, with GroupNorm and a swish gate, make retention competitive with attention.",
      "At 7B scale and 8k length, RetNet decodes 8.4x faster and saves 70% of memory compared with a Transformer using KV caches.",
      "RetNet's perplexity scaling is competitive with Transformers above roughly 2B parameters."
    ],
